      "body": "## Description\nFixes #8537.\n\n### Problem\n`delete_cuda_graphs()` relies on `_CudagraphGlobalRecord.cudagraph_record` to locate and reset active `_CudaGraphRunner` instances (`runner.cudagraph_created = False`, `runner.fwd_graph = None`, `runner.bwd_graph = None`, `runner.mempool = None`). However, `_CudagraphGlobalRecord.create_cudagraphs()` clears `cls.cudagraph_record = []` upon completing graph capture. Consequently, calls to `delete_cuda_graphs()` after graph capture encounter an empty `cudagraph_record` and fail to reset the runners, retaining graph and mempool references and leading to process termination hangs (e.g., in Megatron-Bridge recipes, see https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/issues/6639 and WAR PR https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/pull/6681).\n\n### Solution\n1. In `_CudagraphGlobalRecord.create_cudagraphs`, retain captured runners in `_CudagraphGlobalRecord.cudagraph_created_runners` before resetting `cudagraph_record`.\n2. In `delete_cuda_graphs()`, aggregate runners from `cudagraph_created_runners` along with any un-captured and inference runners, resetting their state, graph handles, and mempool references.\n3. Added unit tests in `tests/unit_tests/transformer/test_cuda_graphs.py` (`TestDeleteCudaGraphsRunners`) to verify that `delete_cuda_graphs()` properly resets runners and clears global tracking state after capture.\n\n### Testing\n- Verified `test_delete_cuda_graphs_resets_captured_runners` passes and confirms that `runner.fwd_graph is None`, `runner.bwd_graph is None`, `runner.mempool is None`, and `runner.cudagraph_created is False`.\n",
